From bd17733936dfda889e0cf93bb0225d0402b987bb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gili Tzabari <cowwoc2020@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 21:43:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Upgrade direct zbus and isolate Secret Service retirement
 notices

Use zbus 6 for TUI reduced-motion settings with the Tokio backend and
wire variant API. Keep Secret Service credentials supported while its
upstream zbus migration is pending. A WORKAROUND links PR 122 and limits
advisory exceptions to the three retired standalone crates.

Refresh Cargo and Bazel resolution. The required Tokio update deprecates
AsyncFd::new, so register the owned PTY and pidfd descriptors through the
replacement API with explicit lifetime safety guarantees.

Base: rust-v0.163.0 (83086188ae0614bd882818ff1aa23f3194962012)
Prerequisites: preceding issue-61 dependency-policy patches.

Red: the all-features dependency graph with the original deny policy
fails exactly RUSTSEC-2026-0370, RUSTSEC-2026-0371 and RUSTSEC-2026-0372.
Green: the maintained all-features cargo-deny check passes, preserving
visible duplicate-version notices and enforcing stale-exception checks.
The complete queue's formatter and Bazel lock check pass in the authoring
tree. Emitted-queue and TUI/PTY suite results are recorded separately in
the owning task's acceptance record.

Fresh emitted queue: all 187 patches apply and 9,361 tracked files match
the tested source, excluding documented workspace version normalization.
Fresh formatting, Bazel lock and full dependency checks pass.
TUI/PTY libraries compile with first-party warnings fatal. All 62 PTY
tests pass. The complete run has 5,802 passing and 50 failing tests;
36 failures pass after clearing terminal variables and shortening TMPDIR.
Fourteen local TUI failures remain for hosted-environment verification;
the complete local suite is not claimed as passing.
